# Paths carried to the hub even though .gitignore / hubignore / the built-in
# excludes would drop them. Committed on purpose: it means the same thing on
# every clone and every machine.
#
# These two hold the project's WORKING MEMORY, and neither is in git:
#
#   docs/         — design specs and implementation plans (gitignored)
#   .superpowers/ — the SDD ledger: per-task findings and the carried
#                   constraints ("never order across machines by pushedAt",
#                   "never floor mtimeMs", "never probe a binary with --help"),
#                   each with the measurement behind it.
#
# GitHub issues carry what to do next. These carry what NOT to do and why we
# know — which is what stops a fixed defect being reintroduced. Losing them on
# a machine move means re-deriving all of it, so they travel with the sessions.
#
# A pattern with a `/` anywhere in it is rooted at the project; a bare pattern
# matches that name at any depth. See README's hubinclude section.
docs/
.superpowers/
